  "id": "Compound::DB00482 - Gene::23632",
  "verbalization": "Celecoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, is shown to bind to multiple calcium-binding proteins (Ca5a, Ca5b, and Ca6), which are involved in the carbonate dehydratase activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the protein Ca14, suggesting a potential mechanistic pathway where Celecoxib modulates the function of calcium-binding proteins, thereby influencing the carbonate dehydratase activity. The evidence from the three paths collectively supports a direct interaction between Celecoxib and Ca14 through a series of molecular interactions involving calcium-binding proteins and their enzymatic activities. The consistent involvement of carbonate dehydratase activity in all three paths indicates a shared biological function, reinforcing the hypothesis that Celecoxib may exert its effects on Ca14 via this pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a plausible mechanism by which Celecoxib could influence Ca14, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the specific role of Ca14 in this process.",
